<title>MEXICO: Mexico's CTM seeks higher wage hike, issues threat.</title>
<headline>Mexico's CTM seeks higher wage hike, issues threat.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fidel Velazquez, head of the powerful Mexican Workers Confederation (CTM), has threatened to withdraw from the National Commission of Minimum Salaries if it fails to approve a hike above 17 percent, newspapers reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The move could undermine one of the key planks of an Alliance for Growth signed between government, business and labor leaders last month, that included agreement on a 17 percent rise in the minimum wage, due to take effect December 3.</p>
</text>
